// @check
// @error a range with `step 0` never advances
// A range `for` whose step folds to 0 never advances its loop variable — a
// degenerate / infinite loop. Refused on D1588's `range-never-runs` category
// beside the direction rule, because both are the same question: a constant range
// descriptor that cannot complete as written. Anchored at the STEP, not the `to`
// — this sentence names `step 0`, so the caret belongs on what must change. The
// bounds need not be constant for it to fire. `_i` is `_`-prefixed so the loop
// variable is not flagged; `loop` is called below so it is not flagged unused.
function loop() {
  for _i in 0 to 10 step 0 {
    print(1)
  }
  return 0
}
print(loop())
